sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgb(232,245,233) Host service
    participant A as Author or approver (REST or Java API)
    participant P as MaskingPolicy (host settings or host bean)
  end
  box rgb(224,242,241) Rule Engine, in process
    participant V as VersionService
    participant C as Masking start-up check
  end
  box rgb(255,248,225) Host PostgreSQL
    participant DB as rle_version, rle_setting_seen
  end
  rect rgb(255,248,225)
    Note over P,DB: Start-up, after the migrations and the masking key check, outside any request
    C->>DB: SELECT the recorded decision-log.mask-default per tenant and for the host default
    C->>P: maskByDefault(tenant) for the host default and every known tenant
    alt the value differs from the one recorded (a new tenant is compared with the host default)
      C->>C: write one host log line naming the tenant, the old and the new value (WARN when masking is turned off)
    end
    C->>DB: upsert the values in force
  end
  rect rgb(224,242,241)
    Note over A,DB: Import, draft replacement or publication request
    A->>V: import kyc-routing (nationalId declares no mask)
    V->>P: requireExplicitMask(tenant)
    alt strict mode on and an input declares no mask
      V-->>A: 422 VALIDATION_FAILED, one violation per input, column nationalId, nothing stored
    else every input declared, or strict mode off
      V->>DB: insert or update the version
      V->>P: personalDataNames(tenant), maskByDefault(tenant)
      V-->>A: the version with warnings: UNMASKED_PERSONAL_DATA nationalId, matched "national id"
    end
  end
  rect rgb(232,245,233)
    Note over A,DB: The approver reviews
    A->>V: GET the pending version, GET the diff against the version in effect
    V->>DB: SELECT both canonical documents
    V-->>A: the same warnings, and masking per input: nationalId MASKED to NOT_MASKED, changed
  end
